# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.

## What this is

Credential Lifecycle Manager (CLM) is a **Nautobot app** (Django plugin) for managing, tracking, auditing, verifying, and reporting on **local credential rotations** across network devices. It is the authoritative source of truth for rotation campaigns, password versions, device credential compliance, rotation history, verification status, and drift detection. It is **not** a PAM solution and stores **no plaintext** — `PasswordVersion` points at a Nautobot `extras.Secret` (Vault-backed) that resolves the value at access time.

The current code in [credential_lifecycle_manager/](credential_lifecycle_manager/) is an **MVP skeleton**: it implements the *shape* of the design (models, driver seam, Celery harness, service layer). Vendor driver internals, migrations, serializers/API, and UI/views are the next build steps (see [README.md](credential_lifecycle_manager/README.md) "Deferred / next steps").

The product and data-model documents are intentionally slightly ahead of the code.
In particular, the approved architecture now includes **frozen campaign scope**,
**campaign targets**, **precheck persistence**, **approval records**, and
**exception tracking**. Those are target structures that should guide new work,
even though they are not fully implemented in `models.py` yet.

